 = Path(args.local_memory_md)\n404:    _append_text(local_memory_path, _markdown_entry(event), header=LOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS)\nCONCLUSIONS\nUse the documented candidate RPC to constrain experiment design: training-fitted ILR locations and Cholesky shapes are controllable, whereas alternative conformal score families, separate group quantiles, structural-zero experiments, and evaluator-side uncertainty instrumentation are not. Investigate training-only residual estimation changes, such as out-of-fold residuals with all-row location refitting, as hypotheses rather than established improvements. Preserve external calibration and fixed row-wise prediction; shape adaptation alone does not establish group-conditional coverage. A correct aggregate evaluation with an overall rubric failure does not identify a protocol defect or a scientific mechanism failure; seek explicit criterion evidence before prescribing repairs. Do not turn a single aggregate selection score into a replicated superiority claim or fabricate uncertainty unavailable from released measurements.\npresentation {'forbidden_visible_terms': ['eligible', 'correct and eligible', 'correctness rate', 'worker_01', 'worker_02', 'combined_score', 'rubric'], 'internal_fields': ['correct', 'eligible'], 'preferred_terms': {'idea': 'model variant', 'ideas': 'model variants', 'implementation': 'configuration', 'implementations': 'configurations', 'program': 'seeded run', 'programs': 'seeded runs'}, 'run_unit': 'seeded_run', 'threshold_rate_rule': 'If a thresholded rate appears in the visible paper, keep one reader-facing meaning per figure, such as target attainment, successful-run fraction, or non-collapse rate. Do not reuse a single label for different task-specific thresholds.', 'variant_unit': 'model_variant'}\nfinal metrics {'combined_score': 0.8835919142358097, 'coverage_gap_vs_euclidean': -0.001440972222222218, 'coverage_gap_vs_ilr': 0.025052083333333332, 'marginal_coverage': 0.8941579861111111, 'normalized_volume':