{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'def generate_raw|family ==|family in|Dirichlet|dirichlet|logistic|shift|C4|C3|C2|C1|BASELINES' task/capture.py task/evaluate.py task/evaluate_final.py task/task_contract.json | head -70; sed -n '1,90p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '1,115p' results/ideas/03_continuous_boundary_covariance_interpolation/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '945,965p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '1195,1218p' task/evaluate.py\"","aggregated_output":"task/task_contract.json:9:    \"description\": \"Investigate whether training-only, input-adaptive ellipsoids in orthonormal log-ratio coordinates improve the coverage-efficiency tradeoff over Euclidean-simplex and isotropic log-ratio split conformal regions, and when that advantage disappears. The response is a genuinely observed random composition, not a categorical label or an unobserved true class-probability vector. Primary cases distinguish interior homoskedasticity, heteroskedasticity, near-boundary compositions, and covariate shift. Compare marginal joint coverage at nominal 0.90, prespecified subgroup coverage, normalized simplex-region volume, point error, and runtime with uncertainty. Exchangeability supports marginal coverage only for the IID cases; neither conditional coverage nor covariate-shift robustness is guaranteed. Results may support, refute, or qualify the efficiency hypothesis. Scope is strictly positive synthetic compositions with K=3 or K=8 and small supervised predictors; no claim about arbitrary real datasets, exact-zero compositions, classification-label coverage, universal dominance, or novelty established by performance alone. Publication conclusions and their uncertainty are assessed separately from search eligibility. Standalone Linux x86_64 CPython 3.12 runtime (draft host 3.12.15, refining planned 3.11), pinned NumPy 2.2.6, no GPU/network/paid API. Native untrusted execution requires Landlock ABI>=1 and seccomp; fresh environment, process group termination/reap, eight-GiB candidate AS, thread-aware CPU and four-core role affinities. Each role uses four CPU cores/eight GiB of aggregate eight cores/16 GiB. Fixed synthetic workloads and protocols, not a paper-quality/novelty oracle. Search correct and final correct independently require scientific execution/integrity and all controls, not coverage or baseline superiority. Claim support is a separate evidence review. Detailed frozen operation counts, controls, normalization, generator, uncertainty, worst cases, timing and limitations are in each private resource manifest. Evaluator-owned baseline productive timings exclude startup/import/reset/output; task imposes no minimum productive-time floor. Corpus RNG repair: independent evaluator-private 256-bit entropy per frozen primary corpus, never the public candidate reset seed; domain-separated parameter/input/response/probe RNGs and private NPZ provenance. Fatal broker transport failures are operational errors with finite retained slots and partial transcripts, not handled candidate protocol failures; primary worker identity survives secondary cleanup failures and overruns.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:117:        \"path\": \"resources/final/C1-1009.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:119:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:123:        \"path\": \"resources/final/C1-2027.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:125:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_co