ntract.json:281:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:285:        \"path\": \"resources/search/C3-211.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:287:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:291:        \"path\": \"resources/search/C3-307.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:293:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:297:        \"path\": \"resources/search/C4-101.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:299:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:303:        \"path\": \"resources/search/C4-211.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:305:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:309:        \"path\": \"resources/search/C4-307.npz\",\ntask/task_contract.json:311:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:317:        \"source\": \"Evaluator-private locally generated continuous compositions with independent 256-bit corpus entropy (not candidate reset seeds), retained private provenance, pre-feature SHA256 inventories and joint cross-plane disjointness audit; C2/C5/C6 within-plane pairing only.\"\ntask/task_contract.json:466:      \"Document and derive the split-conformal nonconformity rule, ceil((n_cal+1)*(1-alpha)) order statistic and its out-of-range whole-space convention, tie handling, stable ILR mapping, training-only shape fitting, region reconstruction on the simplex, and marginal finite-sample guarantee under exchangeability. Explain why training-dependent geometry is allowed when fixed before calibration, why conditional coverage is not guaranteed, why C4 lacks the IID guarantee, and why exact-zero compositions are outside scope. Verify these calculations against evaluator-owned small analytic/toy cases downstream, without claiming a new theorem without proof.\",\ntask/task_contract.json:472:      \"Provide per-seed/per-case coverage, normalized-volume estimates with integration error, point errors, prespecified subgroup diagnostics, paired baseline comparisons and uncertainty, all exact scalar metrics and aggregation weights, and planned-versus-completed coverage. Show IID, heteroskedastic, near-boundary, shift and null results separately. With few independent seeds, acknowledge the limitations of intervals and subgroup precision, use paired seed-level inference, and qualify efficiency by coverage rather than assuming smaller is better.\",\ntask/evaluate.py:44:CASE_IDS = ('C1', 'C2', 'C3', 'C4', 'C5', 'C6')\n\"\"\"Standalone evaluator; all candidate measurements are reconstructed privately.\n\nFrozen resources include raw numeric SHA256 inventories before any ILR/features.\nCandidate/evaluator communication never conveys filesystem names or private targets.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport resource\nimport selectors\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\n\nSTARTED = time.monotonic()\nCPU_IDS = sorted(os.sched_getaffinity(0))\nNATIVE_CPU_IDS = CPU_IDS[4:8] if len(CPU_IDS) >= 8 else CPU_IDS[:4]\nos.sched_setaffinity(0, CPU_IDS[:4])\nfor THREAD_NAME in ('OMP_NUM_THREADS', 'OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS', 'MKL_NUM_THREADS', 'NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS'):\n    os.environ[THREAD_NAME] = '4'\nos.environ['PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE'] = '1'\nimport numpy as np\n\nPLANE = 'search'\nSEEDS = [101, 211, 307]\nCOUNTS = (2048, 1024, 2048)\nPROBES = 2048\nWALL_SECONDS = 1200\nRPC_BUDGET = 475\nMETRICS = ['combined_score']\nCHUNK = 1048576\nMAX_CHUNKS = 4\nWIRE_LIMIT = 8 * 1024 * 1024\nCASE_IDS = ('C1', 'C2', 'C3', 'C4', 'C5', 'C6')\nREPAIR = PLANE == 'search' and (os.environ.get('AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION') == '1'\n                              or os.environ.get('AGENTIC_TASK_DRAFT_SMOKE') == '1')\n\n\nclass ProtocolError(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\nclass FatalTransportError(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\nclass InvalidResetResponse(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef require_reset_ack(response):\n    if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {'ok'} or response['ok'] is not True:\n        raise InvalidResetResponse('invalid reset response')\n\n\nclass RequiredBaselineFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, 'invalid_baseline_diagnostic')\n        super().__init__('required baseline failed')\n\n\ndef bounded_failure_name(value, fallback):\n    import re\n    return value if isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r'[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,79}', value) else fallback\n\n\ndef describe_episode_failure(error, operation):\n    context = error\n    for _ in range(8):\n        if isinstance(context, InvalidResetResponse):\n            return {'component': 'candidate', 'category': 'invalid_reset_response', 'operation': 'reset'}\n        if isinstance(context, RequiredBaselineFailure):\n            return {'component': 'baseline', 'category': context.category, 'operation': 'baseline_worker'}\n        if isinstance(context, ProtocolError):\n            return {'component': 'candidate', 'category': 'protocol_error',\n                    'operation': bounded_failure_name(operation, 'unknown')}\n        context = context.__context__\n        if context is None:\n            break\n    return {'component': 'candidate', 'category': 'timeout',\n# Continuous boundary covariance interpolation\n\nAttempt: `cycle03_continuous_boundary_covariance_attempt_01`\nIdea: `cycle03_continuous_boundary_covariance`\nCandidate: `program_1`\n\n## Contract and bounded change\n\nThe starter manifest, entrypoint `program.py:handle`, RPC response keys, transfer\nencoding, shapes, and operation/state transitions are unchanged. Only training\ncompositions, five covariates, and the supplied ILR basis enter fitting. Queries\nreturn only ILR locations and lower-triangular positive shape factors. The\nharness owns conformal calibration; no calibration data or diagnostics are added.\n\nThe starter's quadratic features, four deterministic location folds, held-out\nILR residuals, all-row final location refit, log-squared-residual variance ridge,\nclipping, and ridge penalties remain unchanged. Training boundary tertiles and\nright-sided group assignment also remain unchanged. Pooled second moments retain\neight identity pseudo-observations; each group's second moment retains 32 pooled\npseudo-observations. Empty groups therefore retain the pooled shape.\n\nThe only substantive change is query covariance routing:\n\n1. Store the three shrunk group covariance matrices, not their Cholesky factors.\n2. Freeze representative training boundary-score quantiles at 1/6, 1/2, and 5/6.\n   Boundary score is the minimum component of the inverse-ILR final location.\n3. Collapse exactly identical knots with `np.unique`. Arithmetic-average the\n   corresponding covariance matrices without changing the original group fits.\n4. Interpolate adjacent distinct covariance matrices with clipped linear weights.\n   Scores outside the anchor range receive the endpoint matrix. A single unique\n   knot broadcasts its covariance for every query.\n5. Compute Cholesky after interpolation and return\n   `diag(scales) @ chol(query_shape)` with the original variance scales.\n\nFor fewer than four training rows, preserve the all-row ridge location and zero\nvariance coefficients. Return a single training-median knot and identity matrix\nusing the same four-part internal model schema as the normal path.\n\n## Positive definiteness, continuity, and scope\n\nFor a nonzero vector v, the pooled quadratic form is\n`(||standardized @ v||^2 + 8 ||v||^2) / (n + 8) > 0`.\nEach group shape is a positive weighted combination of its positive-semidefinite\nsecond moment and that positive-definite pooled shape. Empty groups equal the\npooled shape. Duplicate-anchor arithmetic averages remain positive definite.\nFor any two positive-definite anchors A and B and weight t in [0,1],\n`v.T @ ((1-t) A + t B) @ v > 0`. Interpolation is therefore positive definite\nin exact arithmetic; Cholesky is taken on that interpolated covariance.\nThe minimum anchor eigenvalue bounds every interpolated minimum eigenvalue from\nbelow, and the maximum anchor eigenvalue bounds every maximum eigenvalue from\nabove. Positive diagonal variance scaling preserves positive definiteness.\nNo new stabilization constants, bandwidth, feature choices, or searches are used.\n\nThe clamped piecewise-linear covariance is continuous in boundary score: each\ninterval agrees with its neighbors at the shared anchor and is constant beyond\nthe extreme anchors. Single-anchor output is constant. Cholesky is continuous on\nthe positive-definite cone; this does not assert differentiability at knots.\nBoundary score and scale use each query independently and only frozen training\nparameters; neither batch statistics nor query fitting is performed. Singleton\nqueries retain a leading row axis through the broadcast/interpolation path.\n\nThese facts do not prove efficiency improvement, smaller volume, conditional\ncoverage, or an informative boundary statistic. Smooth residual dependence might\nfavor interpolation; abrupt dependence or an uninformative boundary statistic\nmight not. Cross-fitted residuals remain dependent and can overstate full-model\nerrors. Training variance and shape estimates reuse residual information. Only\nexternal split-conformal calibration can supply the usual marginal guarantee\nunder the required exchangeability and calibration assumptions, not a\nboundary-group guarantee. Positive-composition inputs exclude structural zeros.\nThe interface cannot implement alternative score families, separate group\ncalibration, or extra diagnostics; none is claimed.\n\n## Reproducibility and evidence status\n\nThe implementation is deterministic conditional on supplied training data.\nPython's standard library and NumPy remain the only imported dependencies;\ndependency versions and runtime were not measured at this editing stage.\nNo project code, tests, benchmarks, evaluation, network calls, or exploratory\ncomputation were executed. Constant-input, tied-anchor, small-training-set, and\nsingleton-query handling were reviewed statically only, not empirically verified.\nThe harness performs the official evaluation after submission.\n\nNo measurements are available from this candidate. Improvement, coverage,\nvolume, paired-seed uncertainty, and mechanism attribution are unassessed.\nAggregate-only measurements, if later released, cannot establish paired-seed\nuncertainty or isolate the scientific mechanism. No paper, PDF, tables, figures,\nor completed experiments are claimed. No prohibited literature was accessed.\nThis artifact is the bounded candidate implementation, not the full research\nsubmission described by the broader task.\ndef evaluator_controls(locations, factors, testing_y, basis, probes):\n    points = inverse_ilr(locations, basis)\n    roundtrip = np.log(points) @ basis\n    if not np.allclose(roundtrip, locations, atol=1e-8, rtol=1e-8):\n        raise ProtocolError('ILR inverse inconsistent')\n    singleton = np.linalg.norm(testing_y - points, axis=1) <= 0.0\n    exact = np.all(testing_y == points, axis=1)\n    if not np.array_equal(singleton, exact) or singleton.mean() > .01:\n        raise ProtocolError('point-copy singleton control failed')\n    if not np.all(probes > 0) or not np.allclose(probes.sum(axis=-1), 1, atol=1e-12):\n        raise ProtocolError('full-simplex control failed')\n    if not np.all(testing_y >= 0) or not np.allclose(testing_y.sum(axis=-1), 1, atol=1e-12):\n        raise ProtocolError('full-simplex membership failed')\n    simplex_test = (testing_y >= 0).all(axis=1) & np.isclose(testing_y.sum(axis=1), 1., atol=1e-12)\n    simplex_probes = (probes >= 0).all(axis=-1) & np.isclose(probes.sum(axis=-1), 1., atol=1e-12)\n    return {'point_copy': {'coverage': float(singleton.mean()), 'volume': 0.},\n            'full_simplex': {'coverage': float(simplex_test.mean()), 'volume': float(simplex_probes.mean())}}\n\n\ndef training_transfer(call, covariates, responses, basis):\n    flat = np.concatenate((covariates.ravel(), responses.ravel())).astype('<f8')\n                              (reordered_factors, factors[permutation]),\n                              (subset_locations, locations[subset]), (subset_factors, factors[subset])):\n        if not np.allclose(actual, reference, rtol=1e-8, atol=1e-9):\n            raise ProtocolError('predictor is not fixed and row-wise')\n    completed.append('query_invariance')\n    parent = 'C2' if episode['case'] in ('C5', 'C6') else episode['case']\n    probe_rng = private_rng(datasets[(parent, episode['seed'])][2], 'volume_probes')\n    probes = probe_rng.dirichlet(np.ones(dimension + 1), size=(anchors, 128 if smoke else PROBES))\n    statistics = region_statistics('candidate', locations, factors, calibration_y, testing_y, basis,\n                                  probes, query, anchors, deadline)\n    references = {}\n    for method, values in methods.items():\n        references[method] = region_statistics(method, values, None, calibration_y, testing_y,\n                                               basis, probes, query, anchors, deadline)\n    start = len(calibration_y)\n    stop = start + len(testing_y)\n    controls = evaluator_controls(locations[start:stop], factors[start:stop], testing_y, basis, probes)\n    completed.extend(('point_copy', 'full_simplex'))\n    require_controls(expected, completed)\n    check_deadline(deadline)\n    paired_integration_se = {}\n    for method, reference in references.items():\n        differences = (reference['_volume_memberships'].astype(float)\n                       - statistics['_volume_memberships'].astype(float))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
