te.py:853:    expected = {(case, seed) for case in CASE_IDS[:4] for seed in SEEDS}\ntask/evaluate.py:1011:    counts = (64, 64, 128) if smoke else COUNTS\ntask/evaluate.py:1012:    starts = (0, COUNTS[0], COUNTS[0] + COUNTS[1])\ntask/evaluate.py:1247:    expected_slots = len(CASE_IDS) * len(seeds)\ntask/evaluate.py:1301:    training = np.full((COUNTS[0] * 13,), .125)\ntask/evaluate.py:1302:    query = np.full((COUNTS[1] + COUNTS[2] + 64, 5), -.3333333333333333)\ntask/evaluate.py:1303:    start = {'op': 'fit_start', 'n_rows': COUNTS[0], 'composition_dim': 8, 'ilr_basis': basis.tolist(),\ntask/evaluate.py:1351:    episodes = [{'case': case, 'seed': seed} for case in CASE_IDS for seed in statistical_seeds]\ncontract keys ['schema_version', 'canonical_task', 'method', 'candidate', 'evaluators', 'resources', 'data', 'metrics', 'upstream', 'provenance', 'compute', 'protocol', 'feedback', 'publication']\nmethod {'class': 'Geometry-aware split conformal prediction regions for continuous compositional regression, evaluated by a controlled synthetic benchmark', 'description': 'Investigate whether training-only, input-adaptive ellipsoids in orthonormal log-ratio coordinates improve the coverage-efficiency tradeoff over Euclidean-simplex and isotropic log-ratio split conformal regions, and when that advantage disappears. The response is a genuinely observed random composition, not a categorical label or an unobserved true class-probability vector. Primary cases distinguish interior homoskedasticity, heteroskedasticity, near-boundary compositions, and covariate shift. Compare marginal joint coverage at nominal 0.90, prespecified subgroup coverage, normalized simplex-region volume, point error, and runtime with uncertainty. Exchangeability supports marginal coverage only for the IID cases; neither conditional coverage nor covariate-shift robustness is guaranteed. Results may support, refute, or qualify the efficiency hypothesis. Scope is strictly positive synthetic compositions with K=3 or K=8 and small supervised predictors; no claim about arbitrary real datasets, exact-zero compositions, classification-label coverage, universal dominance, or novelty established by performance alone. Publication conclusions and their uncertainty are assessed separately from search eligibility. Standalone Linux x86_64 CPython 3.12 runtime (draft host 3.12.15, refining planned 3.11), pinned NumPy 2.2.6, no GPU/network/paid API. Native untrusted execution requires Landlock ABI>=1 and seccomp; fresh environment, process group termination/reap, eight-GiB candidate AS, thread-aware CPU and four-core role affinities. Each role uses four CPU cores/eight GiB of aggregate eight cores/16 GiB. Fixed synthetic w\ndimensions [('C1', 3), ('C2', 3), ('C3', 8), ('C4', 8)]\nnormalization Finite little-endian float64, fixed coordinate order, signed zero canonicalized to +0, uint32 little-endian row length prefix, SHA256; no rounding. example hashes cover concatenated X,Y; covariates and response separately audited. Numeric normalization precedes ILR/features/split.\nstrata Four fixed covariate strata: X0<0, X0>=0, X1<0, X1>=0. Empty stratum coverage 0. Descriptive only, no multiplicity-adjusted conditional coverage claim.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '635,695p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '772,813p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '1,45p' results/ideas/03_continuous_boundary_covariance_interpolation/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '1,70p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_ilr_residual_geometry/program_1/src/program.py; cat .agentic_paper_workspace.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '635,695p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '772,813p' task/evaluate.py; sed -n '1,45p' results/ideas/03_continuous_boundary_covariance_interpolation/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md; sed -n '1,70p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_ilr_residual_geometry/program_1/src/program.py; cat .agentic_paper_workspace.json\"","aggregated_output":"    logits -= logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    components = np.exp(logits)\n    return components / components.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n\n\ndef features(covariates):\n    columns = [np.ones(len(covariates))]\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, index] for index in range(5))\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, index] ** 2 for index in range(5))\n    columns.extend(covariates[:, first] * covariates[:, second]\n                   for first in range(5) for second in range(first))\n    return np.column_stack(columns)\n\n\ndef ridge(design, targets):\n    return np.linalg.solve(design.T @ design + 0.01 * np.eye(design.shape[1]), design.T @ targets)\n\n\ndef baseline_worker():\n    request = parse_json(sys.stdin.buffer.readline(WIRE_LIMIT))\n    try:\n        resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_AS, (8 * 1024**3, 8 * 1024**3))\n        limit = cpu_limit_seconds(request['work_seconds'], 4)\n        resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CPU, (limit, limit))\n        covariates = decode(request['x'])\n        responses = decode(request['y'])\n        query = decode(request['query'])\n        basis = ilr_basis(responses.shape[1])\n        productive_began = time.monotonic()\n        cut = 3 * len(covariates) // 4\n        targets = np.log(responses) @ basis if request['method'] == 'ilr' else responses\n        coefficients = ridge(features(covariates[:cut]), targets[:cut])\n        prediction = features(query) @ coefficients\n        if request['method'] == 'euclidean':\n            prediction = np.maximum(prediction, 1e-12)\n            prediction /= prediction.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        productive_seconds = time.monotonic() - productive_began\n        sys.stdout.buffer.write(bounded_json_line({'prediction': encode(prediction),\n                                                 'productive_seconds': productive_seconds}))\n        sys.stdout.buffer.flush()\n    except Exception as error:\n        if PLANE == 'search' and request.get('repair'):\n            report_worker_exception(error)\n        else:\n            print('baseline_worker_failure', file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n        raise SystemExit(1)\n\n\ndef run_baseline(method, covariates, responses, query, deadline, record):\n    interpreter, environment = candidate_subprocess_settings(os.environ)\n    worker = Worker([interpreter, '-I', '-u', str(Path(__file__).absolute()), '--baseline-worker'], environment)\n    failed = True\n    diagnostic = None\n\n    def category():\n        status = worker.process.poll()\n        if status is not None and status != 0:\n            return 'baseline_signal' if status < 0 else 'baseline_exit'\n        return None\n\n    def note(value):\n                            + b'\\0' + private_entropy).digest()\n    return np.random.default_rng(int.from_bytes(digest, 'little'))\n\n\ndef generate_raw(family, counts, *, private_entropy):\n    training, calibration, testing = counts\n    rows = sum(counts)\n    size = 3 if family <= 2 else 8\n    parameter_rng = private_rng(private_entropy, f'family{family}/parameters')\n    input_rng = private_rng(private_entropy, f'family{family}/covariates')\n    response_rng = private_rng(private_entropy, f'family{family}/responses')\n    covariates = input_rng.normal(size=(rows, 5))\n    if family == 4:\n        covariates[training + calibration:, 0] += 1.5\n        covariates[training + calibration:, 1] *= 1.5\n    coefficients = parameter_rng.normal(0, .35, size=(5, size - 1))\n    mean = covariates @ coefficients + .2 * covariates[:, :1] ** 2\n    if family <= 2:\n        scale = np.full((rows, size - 1), .35)\n        if family == 2:\n            scale *= np.exp(.65 * np.clip(covariates[:, :1], -3, 3))\n            scale *= np.linspace(.5, 1.5, size - 1)\n        coordinates = mean + scale * response_rng.normal(size=mean.shape)\n        responses = inverse_ilr(coordinates, ilr_basis(size))\n    else:\n        if family == 3:\n            mean[:, 0] += 2.3\n        proportions = inverse_ilr(mean, ilr_basis(size))\n        concentration = np.maximum(proportions * (3 if family == 3 else 14), .15)\n        responses = response_rng.gamma(concentration)\n        invalid = (responses <= 0).any(axis=1) | ~np.isfinite(responses).all(axis=1)\n        for _ in range(16):\n            if not invalid.any():\n                break\n            responses[invalid] = response_rng.gamma(concentration[invalid])\n            invalid = (responses <= 0).any(axis=1) | ~np.isfinite(responses).all(axis=1)\n        if invalid.any():\n            raise ValueError('invalid synthetic draw')\n        responses /= responses.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    if (responses <= 0).any() or not np.isfinite(responses).all():\n        raise ValueError('invalid composition')\n    return covariates.astype('<f8'), responses.astype('<f8')\n# Continuous boundary covariance interpolation\n\nAttempt: `cycle03_continuous_boundary_covariance_attempt_01`\nIdea: `cycle03_continuous_boundary_covariance`\nCandidate: `program_1`\n\n## Contract and bounded change\n\nThe starter manifest, entrypoint `program.py:handle`, RPC response keys, transfer\nencoding, shapes, and operation/state transitions are unchanged. Only training\ncompositions, five covariates, and the supplied ILR basis enter fitting. Queries\nreturn only ILR locations and lower-triangular positive shape factors. The\nharness owns conformal calibration; no calibration data or diagnostics are added.\n\nThe starter's quadratic features, four deterministic location folds, held-out\nILR residuals, all-row final location refit, log-squared-residual variance ridge,\nclipping, and ridge penalties remain unchanged. Training boundary tertiles and\nright-sided group assignment also remain unchanged. Pooled second moments retain\neight identity pseudo-observations; each group's second moment retains 32 pooled\npseudo-observations. Empty groups therefore retain the pooled shape.\n\nThe only substantive change is query covariance routing:\n\n1. Store the three shrunk group covariance matrices, not their Cholesky factors.\n2. Freeze representative training boundary-score quantiles at 1/6, 1/2, and 5/6.\n   Boundary score is the minimum component of the inverse-ILR final location.\n3. Collapse exactly identical knots with `np.unique`. Arithmetic-average the\n   corresponding covariance matrices without changing the original group fits.\n4. Interpolate adjacent distinct covariance matrices with clipped linear weights.\n   Scores outside the anchor range receive the endpoint matrix. A single unique\n   knot broadcasts its covariance for every query.\n5. Compute Cholesky after interpolation and return\n   `diag(scales) @ chol(query_shape)` with the original variance scales.\n\nFor fewer than four training rows, preserve the all-row ridge location and zero\nvariance coefficients. Return a single training-median knot and identity matrix\nusing the same four-part internal model schema as the normal path.\n\n## Positive definiteness, continuity, and scope\n\nFor a nonzero vector v, the pooled quadratic form is\n`(||standardized @ v||^2 + 8 ||v||^2) / (n + 8) > 0`.\nEach group shape is a positive weighted combination of its positive-semidefinite\nsecond moment and that positive-definite pooled shape. Empty groups equal the\npooled shape. Duplicate-anchor arithmetic averages remain positive definite.\n\"\"\"Training-only boundary-adaptive ILR ellipsoid predictor, finite JSON RPC v1.\n\nAll operations return EXACTLY the keys described here; extra keys are forbidden.\nNo paths, metrics, test targets, calibration responses, or plane identity are inputs.\nSeeds initialize randomness only; accept any nonnegative signed-64-bit integer seed.\nreset {op,seed} -> {ok:true}: discard model and both in-memory transfer buffers.\n\nfit_start {op,n_rows,composition_dim,ilr_basis,alpha,nbytes,chunks} -> {ok:true}:\none training phase per reset; 1<=n_rows<=4096, K=composition_dim in {3,8},\nalpha=0.1, ilr_basis is K by K-1 orthonormal contrast matrix. Training consists\nof row-major float64 X[n_rows,5], then Y[n_rows,K] (positive, row sums one).\nnbytes=8*n_rows*(5+K), chunks=ceil(nbytes/1048576), at most four chunks.\nfit_chunk {op,index,block} -> {ok:true}: consecutive zero-based indices only.\nfit_commit {op} -> {ok:true}: require all bytes; fit actual predictor, free upload.\nAll training inputs are authorized; calibration is performed by the evaluator.\n\npredict_start {op,x:block} -> {n_rows,dimension,nbytes,chunks,encoding,dtype,shape}:\nrequires committed fit and no live prediction. X has shape [N,5], 1<=N<=5952.\nReturn dimension d=K-1; buffer is row-major float64 [N,d+d*d], location first,\nthen a FULL row-major lower triangular Cholesky factor of a positive shape.\nshape=[N,d+d*d], encoding='base64', dtype='<f8', nbytes=8*N*(d+d*d),\nchunks=ceil(nbytes/1048576)<=4. A prediction must be a fixed row-wise function\nof X after fit: no test-time updating, batch position, or batch-size dependence.\npredict_chunk {op,index} -> {block}: ordered chunks of flattened output.\npredict_release {op} -> {ok:true}: requires all chunks read; erase output buffer.\nThe evaluator performs three prediction transfers: full authorized query batch,\nreordered query subset, and another subset, without revealing partition boundaries.\n\nEvery block has EXACT keys {encoding,dtype,shape,nbytes,data}: base64 ASCII data,\nencoding='base64', dtype='<f8', shape a positive integer list, nbytes=8*prod(shape).\nChunk blocks use shape [number_of_float64_values], at most 1048576 raw bytes.\nAll numeric values must be finite. Location and factor magnitudes <=1e6;\nfactor diagonals >=1e-8; singular-value condition number <=1e10.\nAt most 4 MiB per logical buffer, 512 MiB total candidate-owned memory allowed;\ncomplete framed UTF-8 JSON messages <8 MiB (and always <64 MiB). No disk exchange.\nNo optional response keys or candidate diagnostics are supported. Errors are protocol\nfailures, not a channel for scientific self-reports. Reset is the only restart.\nEvaluator controls include matched constant inputs, genuine training derangement,\nactual point-copy singleton/full-simplex membership, query invariance, and replay.\nNeither nominal coverage nor superiority is an eligibility gate: negative results\nare valid when execution and required instrumentation are valid. Search utility is\n1 - .8*max(0,.9-coverage)/.9 - .2*normalized_volume, equally weighted case then seed.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\nCHUNK = 1048576\nSTATE = {}\n\n\ndef decode(block):\n    if set(block) != {'encoding', 'dtype', 'shape', 'nbytes', 'data'}:\n        raise ValueError('invalid block')\n    if block['encoding'] != 'base64' or block['dtype'] != '<f8':\n        raise ValueError('invalid encoding')\n    shape = block['shape']\n    if not isinstance(shape, list) or not shape or any(type(size) is not int or size < 1 for size in shape):\n        raise ValueError('invalid shape')\n    size = math.prod(shape) * 8\n    if size != block['nbytes'] or size > 4 * CHUNK:\n        raise ValueError('invalid size')\n    raw = base64.b64decode(block['data'], validate=True)\n    if len(raw) != size:\n        raise ValueError('invalid byte count')\n    array = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype='<f8').reshape(shape)\n    if not np.isfinite(array).all():\n        raise ValueError('nonfinite')\n    return array\n\n{\n  \"global_memory_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261107_044437/investigation\",\n  \"output_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261107_044437/paper\",\n  \"results_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261107_044437/investigation\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"task_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261107_044437/task\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
